{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And they left over</b> — Two times in the Masorah: here and the other: ויותירו כדבר ה׳ (and they left over according to the word of YHWH). There, where they left over according to the word of YHWH, blessing was sent into it; here, where they transgressed the word of YHWH and left over, a curse was sent into it." "<b>And it bred worms</b> — Three times: here, and the other: וירם כבוד ה׳ (and the glory of YHWH was lifted up), and וירם לבם (and their heart was lifted up) — this is arrogance of spirit, and therefore the Shechinah withdrew, as stated: וירם כבוד ה׳ מעל הכרוב (and the glory of YHWH was lifted up from upon the cherub). As we say in the first chapter of Sotah: anyone who has arrogance of spirit, it is as though he pushes away the feet of the Shechinah. And further: וירם לבם (and their heart was lifted up) — as if his heart is lifted up, that he has arrogance of spirit — ירום תולעים (worms shall rise) — and this is what we learned: very, very be lowly of spirit, for the hope of man is maggots."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:14.485692290Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}